up on the shore of the small forecourt. One time, I ended up standing
on the moat. Other times it just looked normal.

> Surely TDT isn't trying to stick us in the wall... are they?

It looks like do_entity() is undoing e_died()'s good work. When it
goes wrong, the screen isn't getting redrawn properly (in my tests,
the cursor was one square away from the location of the @ sign until I
^Red and the @ moved to be under the cursor). I suspect it's a
case of changing the line:

        if(lev1->typ == MOAT) do_entity(etmp1);

to

        if(levl[etmp1->ex][etmp1->ey].typ == MOAT) do_entity(etmp1);

At least, doing so means I'm not getting that behaviour any more, but
I don't know what else it might break :-) I don't claim to understand
too deeply what the drawbridge code thinks it's doing...

